  "body": "## Motivation\n\n`pr_merge.py` gate 6 counted `[codex-auto-fix]`/`[codex-review-fix]` commits by subject prefix and refused to merge above `MIPSTARRE_FIX_CAP` (default 5) with a message naming \"human attention\" as the remedy. On 2026-09-02 that blocked PR #5 \u2014 six hand-authored review-fix commits, every CI context green, review APPROVED with zero unresolved findings \u2014 and the operator escalated to the owner. The count never carried a safety property: gates 3/4 already bind CI and the review to the exact head SHA, and `autofix.sh` reads the same variable to bound its own loop, so the merge-time cap was not an independent bound. An owner-side audit (six read-only lanes, three adversarial refuters) found nothing the refusal protected.\n\n## Description\n\n1. `pr_merge.py`: the fix-lock probe and the merge-base computation gate 7 reuses stay; the `MIPSTARRE_FIX_CAP` read and the count refusal are gone; the count is printed for the record.\n2. `autofix.sh` cap note and `autofix.md` \u00a75 address the operator; the doc now matches the code (the label is not removed).\n3. `.githooks/pre-commit`: the scope-control budget runs before the `MIPSTARRE_SKIP_HOOKS` exit, so a blanket hook skip cannot launder the owner-only override.\n4. `issues-prs.md` \u00a73/\u00a75, `review.md` (merge gate), `meta.md` \u00a71, `personas/main.md`: exactly one owner-gated control (`MIPSTARRE_INFRA_OVERRIDE`); the operator adjudicates; an owner-blocked item becomes a `needs-owner` issue and the session continues.\n5. Worker personas: repair commits use plain `fix(...)` subjects; the `[codex-*-fix]` prefixes are reserved for `autofix.sh` (they made `review.sh` skip PR #5's heads).\n6. `EVOLUTION.md` entry (2026-09-02). The `events.md` disposition lands with the operator's pending telemetry commit.\n\nWorkflow-layer budget: 188 changed lines (limit 400, no override). The next dispatched item after this merges must be mathematics (persona rule).\n\n## Testing\n\n`python3 -m unittest discover -s scripts/tests -p test_github_workflow.py` \u2014 9 tests OK, including a new subtest that six `[codex-review-fix]` commits with full exact-head evidence pass `--check-only`. Pre-commit hook ran the full suite (430 tests OK), `sh -n .githooks/pre-commit`, `bash -n local/bin/autofix.sh`, `py_compile`.\n\n---\nCloses #20\n",
